# The three test tiers, in one place, because two copies drift.
#
# Read by the Makefile (`include tests/tiers.env`) and by
# .github/workflows/ci.yml (sourced into $GITHUB_ENV). Nothing else may spell a
# tier filter; a guard test asserts both readers derive from this file.
#
#   slim          no RequiresService trait          what GitHub runs
#   full-local    everything except Keycloak        a developer's machine
#   full-keycloak everything                        future
#
# VSTest has no trait-ABSENCE operator, so "no trait" is the negated conjunction
# of every known service. That is why AUTONATE_TIER_SERVICES exists beside the
# filters rather than the filters being written out by hand: a service added to
# the list without being added to the slim filter would silently move its tests
# into slim, and a guard test derives one from the other.

# Every service a RequiresService trait may name. A trait carrying anything else
# fails a guard, because a typo would otherwise land its test in slim.
AUTONATE_TIER_SERVICES=Flowable Dapr Keycloak

# Derived from the line above. Kept literal rather than computed because
# `dotnet test --filter` is passed through several layers of quoting and a
# computed string is one shell away from being wrong in a way nothing notices.
AUTONATE_TIER_SLIM_FILTER=RequiresService!=Flowable&RequiresService!=Dapr&RequiresService!=Keycloak
AUTONATE_TIER_FULL_LOCAL_FILTER=RequiresService!=Keycloak
AUTONATE_TIER_FULL_KEYCLOAK_FILTER=

# --- Size pins (#453) ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# What each filter must discover in tests/AutoNate.E2E.Tests. Checked by
# infra/tier-integrity.sh at the end of `make test-full-local`, because a tier
# that silently gets smaller reports success for the wrong reason.
#
# EXACT, not floors. House style (ExecutionOracleSizeTests' 29, the coverage
# ratchet): growth has to be as visible as loss, or the number drifts upward
# and stops meaning anything. When you add tests, move the pin in the same
# commit -- that is the point, not the friction.
#
# Per service as well as per tier, because the tier total cannot see a test
# re-traited OUT of Flowable: it stays in full-local, it just stops needing the
# engine. That is exactly how a live-engine oracle gets quietly defanged.
#
# Measured 2026-09-15 at ddb58e9: 172 + 198 + 1 = 371, + 5 Keycloak = 376.
AUTONATE_TIER_COUNT_FLOWABLE=198
AUTONATE_TIER_COUNT_DAPR=1
AUTONATE_TIER_COUNT_KEYCLOAK=5
AUTONATE_TIER_COUNT_FULL_LOCAL=371
